# Reactive Markdown

This page proves Stage 2 from the original vision: Markdown-native state ships a runtime only when the page asks for it.

:state count = 0

The count is { count }.

:button "Increment" -> count++

:state open = false

:button "Toggle details" -> open = true

:if open
The details are visible now.
:else
The details are hidden.
:endif

:state todos = ["Route pages", "Ship tiny runtime"]

## Reactive list

:for todo in todos
- { todo }
:endfor

:button "Add todo" -> todos += "Live compile"

Static pages like Docs stay runtime-free.

</main>
